From 48dc9256bf4a43f22dbfb0be09f0964537fa6597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 05:08:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Public IDropTarget + nine DataGridView enums

Close ten net48 type gaps. IDropTarget existed only as an empty internal marker,
so a custom drop target (class X : IDropTarget) would not compile; make it public
with the four WinForms notification methods and implement them on ToolStripItem
(which declares the interface) - adding its DragEnter/DragOver/DragDrop/DragLeave
events and the protected OnXxx raisers, with explicit interface members routing
to them.

Add the nine absent DataGridView enums (RowHeadersWidthSizeMode, AutoSizeRowMode,
CellBorderStyle, ClipboardCopyMode, ComboBoxDisplayStyle, EditMode,
HeaderBorderStyle, HitTestType, ImageCellLayout) with the exact underlying values
dumped from the net48 reference assembly - AutoSizeRowMode and EditMode do not
follow declaration order, so the values were verified, not guessed.

Covered by DataGridViewEnumValuesTests (every member value pinned to the
reference) and DropTargetFunctionalTests (interface polymorphism and
ToolStripItem routing interface calls to its drag events). net48 present types
914 -> 924.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
